  "description": "QIQZID crystallizes in the monoclinic crystal system with space group C 2/c. Reported CIF formula moiety: C50 H108 N14 O48 Sm8 2+,2(C2 H3 N1),2(N1 O3 1-). From the CIF bond table, Sm1 (Sm) has 8 O neighbors; Sm2 (Sm) has 8 O neighbors; Sm3 (Sm) has 8 O neighbors; Sm4 (Sm) has 8 O neighbors; Sm1D (Sm) has 8 O neighbors; Sm2D (Sm) has 8 O neighbors; Sm3D (Sm) has 8 O neighbors; Sm4D (Sm) has 8 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 13 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.740-5.564 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 88.22-177.71°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula [Sm8(H2L)4(HL)4(NO3)6(CO3)2](NO3)2·2CH3CN. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 6 NO3 (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 2 NO3 (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 6 NO3 (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)), 2 NO3 (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)).",
